    "insert": "The proposed research will explore the impacts of parasocial interactions with AI agents in augmented reality, focusing on potential benefits of these parasocial aspects on efficiency improvements in completing tasks and learning subjects. It aims to explore different sorts of parasocial interactions, observing the impacts of a variety of \"personas\" the AI agents embody. Furthermore the researchers want to examine how these various roles affect the acceptance of the agents by test participants.\n\nYou provide citations for every claim made, building a strong theoretical foundation for the proposed theories. Furthermore the expose flows well, highlighting the lack of exploration into the topic of parasocial interactions and their impact on augmented reality environments.  This is followed up on with an extensive and well elaborated theoretical underpinning of your proposed research. Finally you provide a well thought out experiment setup, incorporating both qualitative and quantitative methods for evaluating the results of your study.\n\nThe methodology should provide insight into how you want to answer your research questions. It should describe what you want to do, who will be involved and how you want to extrapolate the results into actionable data. Further you should reflect on the limitations of your chosen approach and weigh its benefits and disadvantages. While you methodology is generally very well written and addresses all of these categories, it extensively highlights the limitations of the research. You spend most of the end of your approach section on exploring why the research is limited and that the data is likely to not be representative. Though this is a realistic assessment and shows reflection on your part, it does not inspire confidence in potential readers. I would suggest you incorporate ideas for solving the limitations of your methodology, exploring how you could secure funding or assistance from research institutions or the private sector. This will preserve the reflection on the limitations of your research, while also offering a path to potentially mitigating some of said limitations.\n\nThe project schedule should show in detail what part of the research project should be done at what part of the project. It should be a representation of the original research you want to perform and present a realistic timeline for the steps you want to take in answering the posed research questions. Your schedule seems very realistic overall, incorporating enough time for research, preparation and writing. However some parts seem a bit underdeveloped when compared to the rest of the schedule, making it seems like you don't value them as much. Further there is very little time allocated to literature research, potentially hindering you when actually writing your report later on. I suggest fleshing out the description of  \"Scheduling\", diving deeper into what you will plan, creating more cohesion to the following parts of the schedule. Also i would recommend allocating more time to literature research, adding at least half a week to make sure you cover all relevant parts of contemporary literature.\n\nFinally, there are a few spelling and grammatical errors. I recommend proof reading your expose before final submission, as these errors might make the entire text seems unprofessional."
